  <tei:text>
    <tei:body>
      <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:beit_yaaqov_lekhu">
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:isaiah/2/5"/><tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/1"/>House of Jacob,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/2"/>Come let us walk in the light of Adonoy.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:micah/4/5"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/3"/>For all the nations
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/4"/>walk in the name of its god,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/5"/>but we walk in the Name of Adonoy,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/6"/>our God, forever.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:kings_1/8/57"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/7"/>May Adonoy, our God, be with us
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/8"/>as He was with our fathers,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/9"/>may He not forsake us nor abandon us,
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:kings_1/8/58"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/10"/>that He may turn our hearts to Him,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/11"/>to walk in all His ways,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/12"/>to preserve His commandments, His statutes,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/13"/>and His precepts,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/14"/>which He commanded our fathers.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:kings_1/8/59"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/15"/>May these words of mine
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/16"/>[with] which I have prayed
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/17"/>before Adonoy,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/18"/>be near to Adonoy, our God
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/19"/>by day and night;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/20"/>that He provide the needs of his servant
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/21"/>and the needs of His people Israel
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/22"/>each day.
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:kings_1/8/60"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/23"/>In order that it become known
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/24"/>to all the peoples of the earth
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/25"/>that Adonoy is God—
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:beit_yaaqov_lekhu/26"/>there is nothing else.
<tei:milestone unit="phrase"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse"/></tei:p>
      </tei:div>
